EC2 Access 
1. To access instances, need to generate key and key pair name.. if key is not downloaded then you can't access the instances. 
2. 20 EC2 instances is limit in a region. And to increase number instances per region ,need to request amazon. 

EC2 status check 
1. AWS check instances status every one minute. In order to identify hardware and software issues. 
2. EC2 status is inbuilt in instances. user can't modify and change configuration of EC2 status check. 
3. EC2 is sending metric data to AWS cloudwatch every 5 minutes, which is free , if you want to reduce the time then have to pay . 
4. EC2 instance are not chargeable if it is stop , however you have to pay for the storage i.e hard disk if instance is not terminated. 


Types of root volumes type 
1. EBS stored backed EC2 instance
2. Instance store backed EC2 

Instance store root volums is faster as compared to EBS backed , as instance is directly attached ,whereas EBS is attached to network for example: external hard drive.
-----------------------------------XXXXXXXXXXXX-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
When you stop an EBS Backed EC2 instance?
*Instance perform a shutdown
*State changes from running to stoping
*EBS volumes remain attached to instance
*Any data cached in RAM or instance Store volume is gone/deleted
*Instance retain it's private IPv4 or any IPv6 address
*Instance release public IPv4 to AWS pool
*Instance retain it's elastic IP address. 
Note : Elastic IP - it is static public IP. Need to pay for Elastic IP. If not required need to release Elastic IP. 

EC2 Termination 
* Root volume is deleted automatically when EC2 instance is terminated. 
* Enable EC2 Termination Protection against accidential termination. It is recommeded to always enable to protect accidential termination of instance by trainee 
 
EC2 Metadata : It has instance details such as IPv4, DNS hostname, AMI- ID,instance ID, local hostname
* Metadata can only be viewed within the instance
* Metadata is not protected by encrytion , anyone those have access  to instance can view metadata.
Note : to View metadata
GET http://169.254.169.254/latest/Metadata

Instance user data : it is used to additional patch or command during boot option.
*can be stopped by stopping EC2 first. 
* data is limited to 16 KB, 
*it is not encrypted

