Purchasing options 
* on Demand instance : 
--> It is used when time period for it's utlisation is unknown or for testing purpose. 
--> Need to pay on hourly basics
--> Fixed rate 
--> Recommended for short term workload that can't be interrupted. 
--> Used where workload required dynamic scaling.
Note : Instance can't move from one region to another, but instance can be copy
--> No need for  advanced payment in on demand instance. 

* Dedicated Instance
--> Your dedicated instance is isolated from another dedicated instance
--> On demand instance will not run parallely with dedicated instance, however on demand instance from same account can run with dedicated instance. 


* Dedicated Host 
--> used where lkf required to run on dedicated hardware
--> here you have to pay from host not for instance, we can create as many instance which is allowed by the capacity for host. 

* Spot instance
--> It is cheapest among all other purchasing options . available discount upto 90 % compared to on demand prices. 
--> These are unused instance, they are purchase via biding.
--> Used to testing purchase
--> can be stopped, hibernate or terminate the spot instance
Note : When would my spot instance get interrupted?
Primary reason : capacity requirment for eg : on demand or reserved instance
Secondary reason : if you chose to set a max spot price and spot price raise above this. 

* Schedule instance
--> used for particular time slot on daily ,weeky or monthly basic for one year 
--> You have to pay , if you are using or not. 

* Reserved Instance
--> available for one year to three year by giving advanced payment. 
--> it is cheaper by 75% as compared to on demand instance

Types of Reserved instance 
1. Standard --- 75 % disount , fixed attributes
2. Convertiable--- upto 54 % discount , can change attributes
3. Schedule 

