* Virtual Private cloud ( VPC) : virtual network or data centre for one client. 
--> Private cloud : Cloud owned by company or oganization , private cloud is more secure than public cloud. 
--> VPC is logically isolated. 
--> Max 5 VPC can be created in a region and 200 subnet in 1 vpc.
--> Max 5 elastic IP, can be extended by requesting amazon. 
--> once vpc created DHCP(dynamic host configuration protcol), NACL( Network access control list) and security group will automatically created. 
--> VPC can't migrate from one region to another . 
--> VPC is always created in a region,not in availabity region. 
--> Subnet mask(CIDR) will be  unique for vpc created from one account. however vpc created from different account can have same subnet mask. for eg : vpc 10.0.0.0/16
--> Subnet mask is created in availabity region, not is region .
--> CIDR range can't be changed after VPC creation. 
--> To change CIDR size, create new vpc. 
--> Different subnet within a vpc can't overlap. 
--> We can expand vpc  by CIDR adding new ip address range or secondary CIDR.( except govt cloud and AWS china)
--> NAT gateway created in public subnet but used for private subnet communication . 
--> Router is inside region. 

* Type of VPC
1. Default VPC --
-->default intenet gateway  is defined. 
--> It is created when AWS account is created. 
--> Default CIDR, security group, NACL and routing table settings
2. Custom VPC -- 
-->default intenet gateway  is not defined. But it can be created by user. 
--> CIDR  can be choosen by user


* Important Steps to create VPC
--> create a vpc
--> subnet
--> Internet gateway
--> Routing table

* Compenents of VPC

Public subnet --  if subnet's traffic is routed to Internet gateway, then subnet is called public subnet, if you want your instance in public subnet to communicate with intenet,then it should have public ipv4 address or elastic IP address
Private subnet-- if subnet doesn't have route to intenet gateway,then subnet is called private subnet

Note :  when we create a VPC, you must specify on IPV4 CIDR block between /16 to /28 
Note : First four and last IP of subnet are reserved and can't be used. 
for eg :  10.0.0.0/24

10.0.0.0 -- network id 
10.0.0.1 --reserved for vpc router 
10.0.0.2 -- DNS server
10.0.0.3 -- for further use
10.0.0.255 -- Broadcast address. 

------------------------------XXXXXXXXXXXX-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*Implied Router( Logically router)  and Route Table 
-->  It is central router
--> It connects different availablity zone and connect VPC to internet gateway. 
--> 200 route table in a vpc, can enter 50 entry . 
--> Each subnet must be associated with only one route table at any given time. 
--> If you don't specify subnet to route table association , the subnet will  associated with default VPC route table. 
-->  You can edit main route table , but can't delete main route table , however it can be delete by making one other route table primary. 
--> You can associate muliple subnet to same route table. 

* Internet Gateway 
--> It is a virtual router that connects a VPC  to internet.
--> Default VPC is connect to internet by default.
--> New VPC need to connect to internet .
--> Ensure that your subnet route table point to internet gateway. 
--> It performs NAT between public and private IPV4 address. 
--> It support IPV4 and IPV6 both.

--------------------------------------------XXXXXXXXXXXX-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAT(network address transalation ) Gateways : 
-->  NAT :  It allows private instance to access internet gateway.
--> only elastic iP is used in NAT Gateway where public and elastic ip both can be used in NAT instance.
--> NAT Gateway will always be at public subnet. and need to assign particular public subnet to NAT Gateway
--> NAT gateway is like PA . It used to secure database. 
--> Need to pay for creating and using NAT gateway and also have to pay to processing via NAT gateway
--> Need to assign a particular elastic iP to NAT Gateway at the time of it's creation. 
--> No need to assign public ip to private instance. 
--> Need to update router table after creation of NAT gateway so that private instance have acces to internet gateway. 
--> Deleting a NAT gateway , disassociate it's elastic IP address. but doesn't release the elastic IP address from your account. 

Note : To access internet for private instance , NAT came into picture. 

Security groups :
--> It is virtual firewall at ENI level 
--> upto 5 security group as per EC2 instance interface can be applied . 
--> security group can only have permit rules , can't have deny rules.
--> Stateful ,return traffic of allowed inbound traffic is allowed even if there are no rules to allow it. 

Network Access control list ( NACL) 
--> It is function performed on the implied router. 
--> It provides optional layer of security at router/VPC level. Act as a firewall for controlling traffic in or out of one or more subnet. 
--> Default NACL , by default it all inbound and outbound ipv4 traffic and if applicable ,IPV6.
-->You can create custom NACL and associate with subnet. custom NACL deny all inbound and outbound traffic by default, even though you can enable inbound or outbound traffic.
--> In VPC, each VPC must be associated with NACL , if not associated it will automatically attached with default NACL. 
-->NACL can have muliptle subnet , however one subnet will be attached with one NACL. if subnet is attached with new NACL then previous attachement is released. 
--> NACL contains as numbered list of rules that we evaluate in order. starting with lowest numbered rule. for eg lower number rule have high priority. 
--> The higest  rule number that you can use for a rule is 32766, recommeded that you create rule with multiple of 100. 
--> It works at subnet level. 
-->NACL are stateless, means inbound and outbound must be explicity allowed . 
--> NACL can have permit and deny rule. 
 
 
* Differnece with security group and NACL

       Security group                                                     NACL
--> Operate at instance level                              --> Operate at subnet level 
--> Support allow rules only                               --> support both allow as well as denny rules
--> Stateful , return traffic is automatically allowed    --> Stateless, return traffic must allowed seperately. 
--> Applies at an instances                                --> Applies to all instance in the subnet. 
--> room,for example                                        --> Main gate for example 


* VPC peering 

--> it will allow communication between two VPC operating on private IPV4 without having access to internet gateway .
--> Instance  in either VPC can communicate with each other as if they are within same network. 
--> You can create VPC peering among your own VPC or with a VPC in another AWS account. VPC can be in different region. 
Note : Transitive Peering : suppose there are 3 VPC , A, B and C. if A is paired with B and B is paired with C. if doesn't means A can communicate with C, different peering is required.














































































































































































 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 




























































































































 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 

































